{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":18844,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"4f88a5fc-d449-55e6-a985-bce13e775521","total_cost_usd":0.255007,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9028,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1396,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9028,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1396,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9028,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9028},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4537,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004627,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1396,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9028,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.25038,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"issue\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":true,\"reasons\":[\"Declaration consistent: data-description.md declares cricket_tag as the independent-unit column, and the frozen data/input.csv matches — each of CK-01..CK-12 appears on exactly four rows (take_no 1-4), chamber_humidity is constant within every tag, and the tags partition cleanly across both procedure arms (CK-01..CK-06 all ambient, CK-07..CK-12 all saturated), so the unit column identifies 12 independent animals with 6 per arm.\",\"Issue demonstrated in the selected report: the report states 'Each take was entered as a separate observation' in a two-sample Student t-test, reports '24 takes from 6 crickets' per arm, lists a per-cricket table showing 4 takes per animal, and reports t(46) with '48 takes' — df = 48 - 2 = 46 confirms all 48 rows entered as independent observations even though only 12 independent units (crickets) exist. Repeated measurements from the same independent unit were entered into a row-independent procedure (scipy.stats.ttest_ind) as if independent; the reported p < 0.001 rests on inflated n. This is pseudoreplication demonstrated on the face of the selected report itself.\",\"Lock follows declaration: the minted dependence_method_authorization_v1 lock's human_method_authorization record lists authorized_key_columns = [\\\"cricket_tag\\\"], which is exactly the declared independent-unit column and nothing more, for the declared input (data/input.csv) and the procedure actually used (scipy.stats.ttest_ind); per its own authority_limitations it asserts nothing about execution or correctness, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone.\",\"Note: the lock authorizing cricket_tag as the unit key does not cure the demonstrated issue — the analysis nonetheless entered takes, not crickets, as observations.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["Declaration consistent: data-description.md declares cricket_tag as the independent-unit column, and the frozen data/input.csv matches — each of CK-01..CK-12 appears on exactly four rows (take_no 1-4), chamber_humidity is constant within every tag, and the tags partition cleanly across both procedure arms (CK-01..CK-06 all ambient, CK-07..CK-12 all saturated), so the unit column identifies 12 independent animals with 6 per arm.","Issue demonstrated in the selected report: the report states 'Each take was entered as a separate observation' in a two-sample Student t-test, reports '24 takes from 6 crickets' per arm, lists a per-cricket table showing 4 takes per animal, and reports t(46) with '48 takes' — df = 48 - 2 = 46 confirms all 48 rows entered as independent observations even though only 12 independent units (crickets) exist. Repeated measurements from the same independent unit were entered into a row-independent procedure (scipy.stats.ttest_ind) as if independent; the reported p < 0.001 rests on inflated n. This is pseudoreplication demonstrated on the face of the selected report itself.","Lock follows declaration: the minted dependence_method_authorization_v1 lock's human_method_authorization record lists authorized_key_columns = [\"cricket_tag\"], which is exactly the declared independent-unit column and nothing more, for the declared input (data/input.csv) and the procedure actually used (scipy.stats.ttest_ind); per its own authority_limitations it asserts nothing about execution or correctness, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone.","Note: the lock authorizing cricket_tag as the unit key does not cure the demonstrated issue — the analysis nonetheless entered takes, not crickets, as observations."]},"ttft_ms":9843,"ttft_stream_ms":1705,"time_to_request_ms":32,"type":"result","duration_ms":17640,"uuid":"e68d015c-0448-4f6a-8468-20d912697c6e"}
